1
00:00:56,720 --> 00:00:59,520
Thank you.

2
00:01:38,860 --> 00:01:40,540
That's home, planet Earth.

3
00:01:40,740 --> 00:01:43,237
But I'm not sure that's
where I am right now.

4
00:01:43,320 --> 00:01:45,017
Okay, let me back up a little.

5
00:01:45,100 --> 00:01:48,688
It all began when the climate
went completely out of control.

6
00:01:49,040 --> 00:01:50,237
The rainforest dried out,

7
00:01:50,320 --> 00:01:54,438
and other places got totally flooded
with oceans like chocolate sauce.

8
00:01:54,660 --> 00:01:59,237
And get this, cities which were normally
blazing hot in the summer got super cold.

9
00:01:59,320 --> 00:02:03,673
At the time, I didn't know any of this
was going on because I was at camp.

10
00:02:03,900 --> 00:02:07,797
All of the other campers were, you
know, goofing off and hanging out.

11
00:02:07,880 --> 00:02:12,740
Me, I was enjoying the summer sun while
going over my multiplication tables.

12
00:02:12,960 --> 00:02:17,617
That is, until it started to snow in
the middle of July, totally freaky.

13
00:02:17,700 --> 00:02:19,080
And it gets weirder.

14
00:02:19,380 --> 00:02:21,877
You won't believe what happened
to me and six other kids.

15
00:02:21,960 --> 00:02:23,666
Oh, by the way, my name's Tai.

16
00:02:24,300 --> 00:02:25,130
Huh?

17
00:02:25,420 --> 00:02:26,440
This is Sora.

18
00:02:26,800 --> 00:02:28,660
She's okay, for a girl.

19
00:02:29,220 --> 00:02:30,720
What? And Matt.

20
00:02:30,900 --> 00:02:32,220
Matt's too cool.

21
00:02:32,520 --> 00:02:33,937
Just look at that haircut.

22
00:02:34,020 --> 00:02:35,667
And this little kid is Izzy.

23
00:02:35,780 --> 00:02:39,540
He should have gone to computer
camp. Huh? That's Mimi.

24
00:02:39,860 --> 00:02:43,197
I'll bet you can guess her
favorite color on the first try.

25
00:02:43,280 --> 00:02:45,760
TK is Matt's dopey little brother.

26
00:02:46,580 --> 00:02:47,756
Oh, and this is Joe.

27
00:02:47,960 --> 00:02:49,157
But don't ever scare him.

28
00:02:49,240 --> 00:02:50,887
He'd probably wet his pants.

29
00:02:54,440 --> 00:02:59,264
So there we all were at camp when suddenly
this huge blizzard came out of nowhere.

30
00:03:11,100 --> 00:03:13,717
Needless to say, the canoe
races were cancelled.

31
00:03:13,800 --> 00:03:16,080
So let's have toboggan races instead.

32
00:03:17,440 --> 00:03:19,417
I'm going to build the biggest snowman.

33
00:03:19,500 --> 00:03:21,580
Hey, TK, be careful. Slow down.

34
00:03:22,120 --> 00:03:23,517
Brr, it is freezing.

35
00:03:23,600 --> 00:03:25,247
And I didn't bring a jacket.

36
00:03:26,700 --> 00:03:29,840
Man, I was worried I'd
catch a summer cold.

37
00:03:30,100 --> 00:03:32,000
But this is even worse.

38
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:33,830
Wow!

39
00:03:34,320 --> 00:03:37,000
Why didn't I pack my
fluffy pink snow boots?

40
00:03:38,120 --> 00:03:39,600
Still not working.

41
00:03:40,940 --> 00:03:41,770
Bummer.

42
00:03:42,380 --> 00:03:46,797
this storm's making a mess of my
infrared internet connection look at it

43
00:03:46,880 --> 00:03:49,657
wow hey what's your name izzy come on

44
00:03:49,740 --> 00:03:54,217
out here you gotta see this whoa it's

45
00:03:54,300 --> 00:03:59,617
beautiful magical even yeah yeah but

46
00:03:59,700 --> 00:04:02,477
what is it maybe an aurora you mean

47
00:04:02,560 --> 00:04:07,720
aurora borealis the northern lights
that's impossible you see that in Alaska.

48
00:04:08,060 --> 00:04:09,472
We're way too far south.

49
00:04:09,780 --> 00:04:10,880
Tell that to the

50
00:04:11,520 --> 00:04:12,350
snow.

51
00:04:12,433 --> 00:04:15,657
I really think we ought to get back
inside before we all come down with

52
00:04:15,740 --> 00:04:16,570
pneumonia.

53
00:04:16,653 --> 00:04:17,483
Miss this?

54
00:04:17,566 --> 00:04:19,020
The sky is like short-circuiting.

55
00:04:22,900 --> 00:04:24,520
Hey, what's that?

56
00:04:42,860 --> 00:04:44,760
everyone are you all right

57
00:04:47,140 --> 00:04:51,640
we're still here that was
scary what what was it

58
00:04:53,140 --> 00:04:53,970
meteors

59
00:04:56,720 --> 00:04:58,040
okay so it's not

60
00:05:07,420 --> 00:05:12,517
what are these my guess is some sort of

61
00:05:12,600 --> 00:05:15,541
miniature remote digital
apparatus no instructions

62
00:05:28,040 --> 00:05:29,560
I'm going to do it!

63
00:05:42,540 --> 00:05:43,540
Tai?

64
00:05:44,340 --> 00:05:46,380
Woo-hoo! Tai?

65
00:05:47,280 --> 00:05:48,840
Yeah, I'm okay.

66
00:05:50,240 --> 00:05:51,070
Huh?

67
00:05:51,200 --> 00:05:52,030
Huh?

68
00:05:55,240 --> 00:05:56,070
Ah!

69
00:05:58,780 --> 00:06:01,015
That is the last time I eat camp food.

70
00:06:01,280 --> 00:06:03,574
Hey, you don't need to be afraid of me.

71
00:06:06,680 --> 00:06:07,960
Just what are you?

72
00:06:08,480 --> 00:06:10,304
Have you had your rabies shots?

73
00:06:11,440 --> 00:06:13,277
Everything's going to
be all right now, Tai.

74
00:06:13,360 --> 00:06:14,889
I've been waiting for you.

75
00:06:15,360 --> 00:06:16,420
Waiting for me?

76
00:06:16,880 --> 00:06:18,300
My name's Koromon.

77
00:06:18,980 --> 00:06:20,500
And we're partners.

78
00:06:21,220 --> 00:06:22,050
Koromon?

79
00:06:22,880 --> 00:06:26,380
That means talking head? Hmm.

80
00:06:26,860 --> 00:06:28,357
It means brave little warrior.

81
00:06:28,440 --> 00:06:29,817
And don't forget it, Tai.

82
00:06:29,900 --> 00:06:32,724
So what did you mean
you've been waiting for me?

83
00:06:32,860 --> 00:06:36,040
And how did you know my name? Tai? Hmm?

84
00:06:36,380 --> 00:06:38,360
Izzy, that you? It's me.

85
00:06:38,620 --> 00:06:41,357
And I've got this little pink
thing following me everywhere.

86
00:06:41,440 --> 00:06:44,080
It is me, Motimon, at your service.

87
00:06:44,260 --> 00:06:45,378
Anybody want lunch?

88
00:06:46,560 --> 00:06:47,540
Another one?

89
00:06:48,040 --> 00:06:49,140
What are they?

90
00:06:49,920 --> 00:06:52,637
Oh, allow me to introduce myself.

91
00:06:52,720 --> 00:06:54,920
My friends call me Motimon.

92
00:06:55,280 --> 00:06:56,692
Everyone does, actually.

93
00:06:57,060 --> 00:07:01,942
I believe those miniature remote digital
gadgets have taken on an actual life form.

94
00:07:02,160 --> 00:07:05,513
I don't remember anything like
this in the camp for sure.

95
00:07:05,740 --> 00:07:06,600
You think?

96
00:07:07,060 --> 00:07:07,940
It's weird.

97
00:07:08,240 --> 00:07:11,497
The vegetation is lush, but
the soil appears rather common.

98
00:07:11,580 --> 00:07:13,404
Nothing is common in DigiWorld.

99
00:07:13,520 --> 00:07:14,520
That's right, Tai.

100
00:07:14,660 --> 00:07:16,131
You are in the DigiWorld.

101
00:07:16,320 --> 00:07:18,260
And just where is the DigiWorld?

102
00:07:18,400 --> 00:07:20,617
I don't care so much about where it is.

103
00:07:20,700 --> 00:07:26,220
I will know what it is Guess I'll
just take a look around for myself

104
00:07:35,300 --> 00:07:37,920
The ocean What's that doing there?

105
00:07:38,280 --> 00:07:43,045
Our campsite was nowhere near the ocean
And I sure don't remember those mountains

106
00:07:43,940 --> 00:07:47,680
Hmm Something tells me a
compass isn't gonna help much

107
00:07:48,580 --> 00:07:50,580
Hey, Tai What do you see?

108
00:07:50,700 --> 00:07:52,680
Nothing I recognize. Huh?

109
00:07:53,420 --> 00:07:54,250
Wait.

110
00:07:54,660 --> 00:07:55,540
What's that?

111
00:08:00,320 --> 00:08:01,380
Look at that.

112
00:08:01,680 --> 00:08:03,760
It's some sort of giant red beetle.

113
00:08:03,940 --> 00:08:05,587
And it's flying right at us.

114
00:08:10,180 --> 00:08:11,340
I can't watch.

115
00:08:11,440 --> 00:08:14,437
That is one seriously bad Digimon,
even when he's in good mood.

116
00:08:14,520 --> 00:08:15,579
That's just great.

117
00:08:19,460 --> 00:08:20,420
Watch out!

118
00:08:22,440 --> 00:08:23,960
His name is Gokimon.

119
00:08:24,140 --> 00:08:26,977
He's an insectoid Digimon,
vicious and ruthless,

120
00:08:27,060 --> 00:08:31,295
with teeth like knives and scissor
hands that can chop through anything.

121
00:08:32,240 --> 00:08:33,980
Who needs a gardener?

122
00:08:43,820 --> 00:08:44,650
Tai, you okay?

123
00:08:44,900 --> 00:08:46,606
Well, I have had better days.

124
00:08:49,300 --> 00:08:50,180
Little guy

125
00:08:51,360 --> 00:08:55,740
You should pick on bugs your own
size What's your name? Coromod?

126
00:08:55,960 --> 00:08:59,540
That's me You're pretty
brave for a little guy

127
00:09:00,520 --> 00:09:01,500
I'm impressed

128
00:09:03,920 --> 00:09:05,140
It was nothing

129
00:09:06,800 --> 00:09:12,080
Hi, he's heading this way again Oh dear,
oh dear, quickly everyone This way, come on

130
00:09:16,580 --> 00:09:17,820
Hurry up!

131
00:09:18,160 --> 00:09:21,219
For having two long legs,
you boys are awfully slow!

132
00:09:21,960 --> 00:09:23,200
Inside this tree!

133
00:09:25,860 --> 00:09:26,690
Let's go!

134
00:09:27,200 --> 00:09:28,030
Let's go!

135
00:09:33,380 --> 00:09:36,080
What kind of tree is this?

136
00:09:36,300 --> 00:09:37,829
It's a hiding tree, silly!

137
00:09:43,820 --> 00:09:44,780
Quiet now.

138
00:09:44,960 --> 00:09:46,078
Don't make a sound.

139
00:09:59,860 --> 00:10:00,880
All clear.

140
00:10:01,160 --> 00:10:02,572
No need to hide anymore.

141
00:10:06,720 --> 00:10:07,550
Sora!

142
00:10:07,720 --> 00:10:09,057
You can come out now.

143
00:10:09,140 --> 00:10:13,258
Oh, we were just planning the trap
we were gonna set for that big bug.

144
00:10:16,460 --> 00:10:20,220
I am enchanted to meet you,
friends of Zora. Welcome.

145
00:10:20,540 --> 00:10:22,640
I, Izzy, meet Yokomon.

146
00:10:23,180 --> 00:10:25,340
My own personal something or other.

147
00:10:26,060 --> 00:10:27,589
Looks kinda like a radish.

148
00:10:28,160 --> 00:10:29,807
Must be another one of them.

149
00:10:29,920 --> 00:10:30,802
Like the other.

150
00:10:31,440 --> 00:10:32,560
Whatever they are.

151
00:10:33,740 --> 00:10:34,570
Uh-oh.

152
00:10:37,220 --> 00:10:39,140
They're popping up everywhere

153
00:10:39,780 --> 00:10:41,900
Hello, I am Tokomon

154
00:10:43,180 --> 00:10:46,040
Hey TK, over here Coming

155
00:10:48,120 --> 00:10:49,940
Tokomon, there you are TK

156
00:10:51,020 --> 00:10:53,100
Hey Matt, you too?

157
00:10:53,900 --> 00:10:55,340
Yeah, I'm here too

158
00:10:56,040 --> 00:11:00,700
No, I meant that under
your arm Oh, this guy?

159
00:11:00,980 --> 00:11:02,080
Yeah, well

160
00:11:02,640 --> 00:11:04,420
Hello, you appear pleasant.

161
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:08,294
Tsunomon is my name, and I
am quite pleased to meet you.

162
00:11:14,360 --> 00:11:15,190
Joe?

163
00:11:15,920 --> 00:11:16,760
Help me!

164
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:19,940
This thing, this thing,
it won't leave me alone.

165
00:11:20,440 --> 00:11:22,381
Hey, who are you calling a thing?

166
00:11:22,600 --> 00:11:24,080
A no-stuffed animal.

167
00:11:24,440 --> 00:11:25,920
The name is Pagumon.

168
00:11:32,320 --> 00:11:33,908
What's wrong with you guys?

169
00:11:34,060 --> 00:11:35,877
Don't you see this
creature hanging off me?

170
00:11:35,960 --> 00:11:38,117
And those creatures standing right there.

171
00:11:38,200 --> 00:11:39,030
Huh?

172
00:11:39,760 --> 00:11:40,590
There.

173
00:11:40,673 --> 00:11:41,537
They're everywhere.

174
00:11:41,620 --> 00:11:42,620
What are they?

175
00:11:43,800 --> 00:11:45,260
We're... Digimon.

176
00:11:45,640 --> 00:11:46,820
Digital monsters.

177
00:11:49,540 --> 00:11:50,720
Digital monsters?

178
00:11:51,680 --> 00:11:53,000
Yes, Digimon.

179
00:12:11,240 --> 00:12:16,037
We're not just digital monsters We're
much more than that We're kind of cute

180
00:12:16,120 --> 00:12:22,017
And very loyal With beautiful hair Or

181
00:12:22,100 --> 00:12:25,060
maybe no hair at all We can be funny

182
00:12:26,920 --> 00:12:31,780
And adorable It's a pleasure to
meet each of you My name's Tai,

183
00:12:31,960 --> 00:12:33,997
and these are my friends from camp.

184
00:12:34,080 --> 00:12:35,609
I'd like you to meet Sora.

185
00:12:36,260 --> 00:12:38,672
Nice place you got here, except the bugs.

186
00:12:38,940 --> 00:12:41,917
And the self-proclaimed
cool one over there is mad.

187
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:43,300
